    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-finding-the-mistake-in-a-vector-calculation">
        <!--<title></title>-->
        <stack label="stk-finding-the-mistake-in-a-vector-calculation" source="stack/top/2-measurement-and-geometry/12-vectors-ii/03-column-vectors-in-terms-of-unit-vectors/Finding-the-mistake-in-a-vector-calculation.xml"/>
    </exercise>

    <exercises xml:id="exercises-unit-vectors">
        <exercise xml:id="ex-columns-to-ijk">
            <statement><p>Write in terms of <m>\mathbf{i}</m>, <m>\mathbf{j}</m> and <m>\mathbf{k}</m>: (a) <m>\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}</m> (b) <m>\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 3 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix}</m></p></statement>
            <answer><p>(a) <m>6\mathbf{i} - \mathbf{j} + 2\mathbf{k}</m> (b) <m>3\mathbf{j} - 4\mathbf{k}</m></p></answer>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-ijk-to-columns">
            <statement><p>Write as columns: (a) <m>-\mathbf{i} + 5\mathbf{j} + 2\mathbf{k}</m> (b) <m>7\mathbf{j} - \mathbf{k}</m></p></statement>
            <answer><p>(a) <m>\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 5 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}</m> (b) <m>\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 7 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}</m></p></answer>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-combine-a-and-b">
            <statement><p><m>\mathbf{a} = 4\mathbf{i} - 2\mathbf{j} + \mathbf{k}</m> and <m>\mathbf{b} = -\mathbf{i} + 3\mathbf{j} + 5\mathbf{k}</m>. Find (a) <m>\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b}</m> (b) <m>2\mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}</m> (c) <m>\mathbf{a} - 3\mathbf{b}</m>.</p></statement>
            <answer><p>(a) <m>3\mathbf{i} + \mathbf{j} + 6\mathbf{k}</m> (b) <m>9\mathbf{i} - 7\mathbf{j} - 3\mathbf{k}</m> (c) <m>7\mathbf{i} - 11\mathbf{j} - 14\mathbf{k}</m></p></answer>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-drone-total-displacement">
            <statement><p>A drone over a shamba near Nakuru makes the displacement <m>30\mathbf{i} + 40\mathbf{j} + 20\mathbf{k}</m> and then <m>-10\mathbf{i} + 15\mathbf{j} - 5\mathbf{k}</m>, in metres. What single displacement has the same effect?</p></statement>
            <answer><p><m>20\mathbf{i} + 55\mathbf{j} + 15\mathbf{k}</m> metres</p></answer>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-solve-for-x">
            <statement><p>Find the vector <m>\mathbf{x}</m> if <m>2\mathbf{x} + \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 5 \\ -6 \end{pmatrix}</m>.</p></statement>
            <answer><p><m>\mathbf{x} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix}</m></p></answer>
            <solution><p><m>2\mathbf{x} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 - 3 \\ 5 + 1 \\ -6 - 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 6 \\ -10 \end{pmatrix}</m>, so <m>\mathbf{x} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix}</m>.</p></solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-linear-combination">
            <title>Challenge: Building a Vector from Two Others</title>
            <statement><p><m>\mathbf{p} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}</m> and <m>\mathbf{q} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 4 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}</m>.
                <ol marker="(a)">
                    <li><p>Find numbers <m>s</m> and <m>t</m> with <m>s\mathbf{p} + t\mathbf{q} = \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 5 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}</m>.</p></li>
                    <li><p>Show that no numbers <m>s</m> and <m>t</m> give <m>s\mathbf{p} + t\mathbf{q} = \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 5 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}</m>.</p></li>
                </ol>
            </p></statement>
            <hint><p>Use two components to find <m>s</m> and <m>t</m>, then test the third.</p></hint>
            <answer><p>(a) <m>s = 3</m>, <m>t = 2</m> (b) the first two components force <m>s = 3</m>, <m>t = 2</m>, which give a third component of <m>5</m>, not <m>0</m>.</p></answer>
            <solution><p>(a) The first two components give <m>2s + t = 8</m> and <m>-s + 4t = 5</m>. From the first, <m>t = 8 - 2s</m>; then <m>-s + 32 - 8s = 5</m>, so <m>s = 3</m> and <m>t = 2</m>. Check the third: <m>3(3) + 2(-2) = 5</m>. Correct.</p>
            <p>(b) The first two components are the same equations, so again <m>s = 3</m>, <m>t = 2</m>. But then the third component is <m>5</m>, not <m>0</m>. No <m>s</m> and <m>t</m> work.</p></solution>
        </exercise>
    </exercises>

    <axiom component="lesson-plan">
        <title>Differentiation</title>
        <table xml:id="table-differentiation-unit-vectors">
            <title>Differentiation Strategies</title>
            <tabular halign="left" top="minor" bottom="minor" left="minor" right="minor">
                <row header="yes" bottom="medium"><cell>Learner Group</cell><cell>Strategy and Learning Experience</cell></row>
                <row><cell>Struggling Learners (Support)</cell><cell>Give a three-row grid with rows labelled <m>\mathbf{i}</m>, <m>\mathbf{j}</m>, <m>\mathbf{k}</m> to fill in component by component. Focus on activity parts (a) to (d) and <xref ref="example-changing-the-form"/>. Assign <xref ref="ex-columns-to-ijk"/> and <xref ref="ex-ijk-to-columns"/>.</cell></row>
                <row><cell>On-Level Learners (Core)</cell><cell>Full activity plus all examples. Assign <xref ref="ex-columns-to-ijk"/> to <xref ref="ex-solve-for-x"/>.</cell></row>
                <row><cell>Advanced Learners (Challenge)</cell><cell>All exercises including <xref ref="ex-linear-combination"/>. Extension: find the vector <m>\mathbf{c}</m> with <m>\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{c} = \mathbf{0}</m> for <m>\mathbf{a}</m>, <m>\mathbf{b}</m> in <xref ref="ex-combine-a-and-b"/>. (Answer: <m>-3\mathbf{i} - \mathbf{j} - 6\mathbf{k}</m>.)</cell></row>
            </tabular>
        </table>
    </axiom>

